        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): regenerate native hook descriptors when relay unavailable after restart",
        "body": "## Problem\n\nNative hook descriptors were not regenerated when the relay was unavailable during restart, causing hooks to silently fail after gateway restart until manual intervention.\n\n## Root Cause\n\nThe native hook relay regeneration logic in `native-hook-relay-cli.ts` only triggered on initial relay connection, not on reconnection after the relay was unavailable during startup.\n\n## Fix\n\nRegenerate native hook descriptors when the relay becomes available after being unavailable at restart time. This ensures hooks work after gateway recovery without manual restart.\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Test Results (vitest 4.1.8)\n\n```\n$ vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.cli.config.ts \\\n    src/cli/native-hook-relay-cli.test.ts\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  20 passed (20)\n   Start at  20:38:48\n   Duration  5.28s (transform 2.27s, setup 407ms, import 3.75s, tests 916ms, environment 0ms)\n```\n\n### Before/After\n\n**Before:** Relay unavailable at gateway restart → native hook descriptors not regenerated → hooks silently fail.\n\n**After:** Relay becomes available after restart → descriptors are regenerated automatically → hooks work without manual intervention.\n\nFixes #89325",
